# Lessons Learned

This workspace holds the **Portfolio** project: Jamie Tucker's recruiter-facing
software engineering portfolio. A sibling folder, `PersonalWebsite`, holds a
separate Y2K-styled creative site (music, reels, photos). They share conventions,
not content or aesthetics — do not mix their patterns.

## Portfolio patterns (this project)

- **Milestone 6 (shipped 2026-08-06):** three major sections — `#about` →
  `#experience` → `#contact`. Role and contact content use YouTube-inspired
  **pill boxes** (`.pf-pill-box`); About uses `pro_headshot.jpeg` and a Matt
  Farley–style triad with proof metrics as bullets; structural styling evokes
  early-2010s YouTube (`--pf-card-shadow`, denser masthead) while **OSU
  scarlet/gray/white tokens stay locked**. Soft-alias retired hashes via
  `SiteNav.HASH_ALIASES` + `setupHashAliases`. Pill copy lives in
  `utils/role-pills.js` (tested). Filters are gone from the page.
- **The site is one page.** `index.html` holds About, Experience, and Contact.
  `utils/site-nav.js` is the section model — add a section there, in the markup,
  and in the nav, or the markup test fails.
- **Three layers, one direction**: `utils/` (UMD data + pure logic) → `pages/shared/`
  (tokens + chrome) → `pages/index/` section CSS and JS. Nothing lower depends on
  anything higher.
- **Design tokens**: every `--pf-*` token lives in `pages/shared/css/theme.css`. Link
  order is `theme.css` → `layout.css` → `pages/index/css/*.css`.
  Page CSS consumes tokens and never redeclares them. New colour = new token in both
  the `[data-theme='dark']` and `[data-theme='light']` blocks.
- **Brand palette is Ohio State**: scarlet `#ba0c2f`, gray `#a7b1b7`, white `#ffffff`
  (plus BUX shades) as raw `:root` tokens. Never use a raw brand token in page CSS —
  map it to a semantic token first, or one theme will break.
- **Accent text and filled controls are different tokens.** `--pf-accent` is
  theme-aware text colour (a scarlet tint in dark mode, because plain scarlet is
  2.7:1 on dark ink). Anything that puts white text on a colour must use
  `--pf-accent-solid`. Getting this wrong is the single easiest way to ship an
  unreadable button.
- **Contrast is enforced, not eyeballed.** `utils/color-contrast.js` mirrors the
  resolved token values and `test/color-contrast.test.js` audits every rendered pair
  at WCAG 2.1 AA (4.5:1 text, 3:1 non-text). Change a colour in CSS *and* in the
  module, together. Decorative hairlines are 1.4.11-exempt; control borders are not.
- **No Tailwind, no CDN CSS, no build step.** A hiring page must render correctly
  with zero third-party scripts. (The sibling project's Tailwind habits do not apply.)
- **Content lives in HTML, data lives in `utils/`.** Pages are hand-written so they
  render with JavaScript off; `utils/resume-data.js` and `utils/project-data.js` are
  the canonical record. `test/page-markup.test.js` fails when the two drift, which is
  what makes the duplication safe.
- **Root `index.html` is the whole site** so the recruiter URL is `/`; each
  section keeps its own stylesheet under `pages/index/css/` (`about.css`,
  `work.css`, `skills.css`, `contact.css`) so the CSS stays as separable as the
  sections.
- **UMD for anything testable.** Pure helpers export to `module.exports` and to a
  browser global (`window.SiteNav`, `window.ResumeData`, …), so Node suites and pages
  share one implementation. Cross-module deps are injected in the wrapper body.
- **Gate every hiding rule behind `.pf-js`** (added by `theme-init.js`), so no-JS
  visitors never lose content.
- **Progressive enhancement for interaction.** Filters read tags from the DOM,
  ship `hidden`, and are unhidden by script. An unknown tag returns *all* items.
- **Data-attribute contracts** for behaviour (`data-nav-key`, `data-section`,
  `data-role-tags`, `data-project-tags`, `data-tech`, `data-copy-email`) so
  refactoring class names never breaks JavaScript.
- **Scope every shared hook to its own container.** Two sections on one page use
  `data-filter-chips`; a `document.querySelector` would hand the second one the
  first one's node. Query from the section container down, always.
- **Class prefixes follow the block that owns the markup.** When a block moves,
  rename it (`exp-role` → `home-role`) in the same commit and let
  `page-markup.test.js` assert the old prefix is gone; a stale prefix sends the
  next reader looking for a page that no longer exists. Section prefixes
  (`about-`, `proj-`, `skills-`, `contact-`) now name sections, not pages.
- **One `h1` per document.** Folding pages together means every former page `h1`
  becomes the `h2` that opens its section, and ids have to stay unique — both are
  asserted.
- **One source for sticky offsets.** `--pf-header-h` in `theme.css` feeds both the
  header's own height and anything that sticks below it, plus the
  `scroll-margin-top` that keeps jump links from landing behind the chrome.
- **Enhancement controls ship `hidden`.** A collapse button is a lie without
  JavaScript, so the markup ships it hidden with all content visible and the
  script unhides it. Note `.pf-btn` sets `display: inline-flex`, which beats the
  `hidden` attribute — add an explicit `[hidden] { display: none }` guard.
- **No `auto-fit` for card grids.** `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(...))` picks a column
  count from available width and regularly strands one card alone on the last row.
  Pin the column count per breakpoint, and let a trailing card at an odd index
  span `1 / -1`. When JS filters a grid, mark the last *visible* card — CSS
  `:last-child` counts hidden ones.
- **Role-pill logo chrome is the template for brand marks in pills.** Education
  had an empty grid cell above affiliations because the OSU logo sat on its own
  row (`'brand .'`). Put degree, labelled list, and logo on one row; size the
  mark with `object-fit: contain` and the same `max-width: 13rem` as
  `.pf-pill-box__logo`.
- **White-on-dark brand marks need a light-theme twin.** Do not `filter: invert`
  a YouTube wordmark (the play button goes off-brand) or the OSU lockup
  (scarlet Block O would invert). Put both SVGs in the markup and let
  `[data-theme]` show one. Prefer a provided light/dark pair that already
  shares a viewBox (OSU) over locking `aspect-ratio` in CSS.
- **Honest content only.** Every home page metric traces to a résumé bullet in the
  home timeline; skill depth is labelled daily driver / production / working
  knowledge rather than invented percentages. Availability wording must match the
  actual end date of the most recent role.
- **Universal font stack**: Inter as a progressive enhancement over the system UI
  fonts, base `1.0625rem` at `1.65` line height, `68ch` measure.

## User preferences

- Follow the Memory Files workflow in `.cursor/rules/memory.mdc` plus the plan and
  implement rules; update `docs/` and `tasks/` in the same session as the code.
- Update `tasks/changelog.md`, `tasks/tasks_plan.md`, and `tasks/active_context.md`
  whenever work ships.
- Feature overviews in `docs/` stay ≤500 words and include a Mermaid diagram;
  standalone diagram sources belong in `diagrams/`.
- Prefer parallel commits for independent concerns (data layer vs chrome vs pages vs
  docs) over one large commit.
- Every new feature needs at least one unit test covering its edge cases, in `test/`.
- Node is v16 locally: no `node:test`, use the harness in `test/lib/test-runner.js`.

## Critical paths

- Recruiter journey: `#about` (headshot + résumé + triad) → `#experience`
  (three role pills + compact skills) → `#contact` (LinkedIn, then email)
- Nav: `utils/site-nav.js` `SECTIONS` + `HASH_ALIASES` → `site.js`
  `setupHashAliases` + scroll-spy → `[data-nav-key]` / `[data-section]`
- Theme: `utils/theme-preference.js` → `theme-init.js` → `theme.css` (**do not
  rewrite brand colours without contrast tests**)
- Role pills: `utils/role-pills.js` → Experience markup → `test/role-pills.test.js`
  + `page-markup.test.js`
- Content integrity: `utils/resume-data.js` (`APPROACH_TRIAD`, `photoPath`) →
  `test/page-markup.test.js`
- Colour integrity: `theme.css` ↔ `utils/color-contrast.js` →
  `test/color-contrast.test.js`
- Headshot contract: `PROFILE.photoPath` → `/media/images/pro_headshot.jpeg`
